rding to the functional equation:\n   \\[\n   f(f(n)) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n\n2. **Analyze the fixed point:**\n   We have:\n   \\[\n   f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n   This suggests that \\( 6n - 2005 \\) is a fixed point of the function \\( f \\).\n\n3. **Check the form of \\( f(x) \\):**\n   Since \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\), we hypothesize that \\( f(x) \\) might be a linear function. Let:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = ax + b\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( f(x) = ax + b \\) into the functional equation:\n   \\[\n   f(f(x)) = f(ax + b) = a(ax + b) + b = a^2x + ab + b\n   \\]\n   According to the given equation:\n   \\[\n   a^2x + ab + b = 6x - 2005\n   \\]\n   By comparing coefficients, we get:\n   \\[\n   a^2 = 6 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad ab + b = -2005\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve for \\( a \\) and \\( b \\):**\n   From \\( a^2 = 6 \\), we have:\n   \\[\n   a = \\sqrt{6} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a = -\\sqrt{6}\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( a = \\sqrt{6} \\) into \\( ab + b = -2005 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{6}b + b = -2005 \\implies b(\\sqrt{6} + 1) = -2005 \\implies b = \\frac{-2005}{\\sqrt{6} + 1}\n   \\]\n   Rationalize the denominator:\n   \\[\n   b = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{(\\sqrt{6} + 1)(\\sqrt{6} - 1)} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{6 - 1} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{5} = -401(\\sqrt{6} - 1)\n   \\]\n\n","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,729,400,69,2075,15087,67901,198,78045,69,955,2075,593,284,220,21,87,481,220,17,15,15,20,59,60,1958,678,1931,5109,400,87,2418,220,2619,6724,458,7546,400,77,3,1741,429,400,69,1445,8,284,220,21,77,481,220,17,15,15,20,2418,220,7379,400,77,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198,1249,11625,369,17767,308,1124,8,1741,429,17767,282,1445,8,284,220,21,77,481,220,17,15,15,20,1124,8,2661,279,15629,23606,17767,282,955